      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "NOT SO DUBIOUS (2) is the one to beat fresh, with his third in a BM66 at Grafton two runs back reading strongly for this grade and Jodi Worley having already won on him. His final run in Quality company was plain, but the drop back to a BM50 and a wet-track record of one win and one placing from five starts give him the right profile. SHE'S A WILD ONE (4) arrives in winning form after putting three and a half lengths on them at Wauchope, and her narrow Class 1 second at Bowraville beforehand adds substance. BRING IT ON SAL (9) is lightly raced and comes off a first-up Mdn win on heavy ground, with Luke Rolls another plus. BIANCO NERO (8) has been in the market at her last couple of starts but hasn't made an impression, last start running sixth at Kempsey. Has upside and expected to be in the finish this time.",
